  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So this random irritating glitch has been happening to me for a long while (long long while, at least a year) what happens is I'm loaded in a world, but after some time passing (usually after at least 15 - 20 minutes) others' voices start stuttering/cutting out to the point of silence, and also that virtually no one can hear me either. And another thing, as it happens, everyone starts looking really stuttery/laggy in their movements. (I.e looking left/right or moving forward/backwards) Ping is fine, frames are fine, but always happens no matter what after some time of joining/rejoining a world. Edit, added pic, delay at right of menu starts at .3 for everyone (minus me of course) but gradually rises nonstop till it's past 2.4 in which all player voices are pure silent and everyone's movement's are choppy. I've tried most if not all remedies to try and fix it I could think of and could search.",
